{
  "title": "Dua of a Mother for Her Ailing Child",
  "data": "Mother's Dua for an Ailing Child\nWhen a child is ill, the mother goes up onto a roof, uncovers her hair under the sky, prostrates and recites:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ رَبِّ اَنْتَ اَعْطَيْتَنِيْهِ\nALLAAHUMMA RABBI ANTA A'TAYTANEEH\nO Allah, my Lord, You gave him to me,\nوَاَنْتَ وَهَبْتَهٗ لِىْ\nWA ANTA WAHABTAHOO LEE\nand You granted him to me as a gift.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ فَاجْعَلْ هِبَتَكَ الْيَوْمَ جَدِيْدَةً\nALLAAHUMMA FAJ'AL HIBATAKAL YAWMA JADEEDAH\nO Allah, so make Your gift new again today;\nاِنَّكَ قَادِرٌ مُقْتَدِرٌ\nINNAKA QAADIRUN MUQTADIR\nYou are indeed All-powerful, Omnipotent.",
  "tabs": [
    "Al-Fatihah over Water & Alms\nIf you are seriously ill, recite [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) 40 times over a glass of water, then pour the water over your body.\nKeep a measure of wheat near you; give each beggar a measure and ask him to pray to Allah for your cure.\nGive alms for the sick.",
    "Holding the Patient's Right Arm\nHold the patient's right arm and recite [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) 7 times, then recite:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اَزِلْ عَنْهُ الْعِلَلَ وَالدَّاۤءَ\nALLAAHUMMA AZIL A'NHUL I'LALA WAD DAA'\nO Allah, remove from him the ailments and the disease,\nوَاَعِدْهُ اِلَى الصِّحَّةِ وَالشِّفَاۤءِ\nWA A'ID-HU ILAS SIHHATI WASH SHIFAA'\nreturn him to health and recovery,\nوَاَمِدَّهٗ بِحُسْنِ الْوِقَايَةِ\nWA AMIDDAHOO BIHUSNIL WIQAAYAH\nsupport him with good protection,\nوَرُدَّهٗ اِلٰى حُسْنِ الْعَافِيَةِ\nWA RUDDAHOO ILAA HUSNIL A'AFIYAH\nand bring him back to sound well-being.\nوَاجْعَلْ مَا نَالَهُ فِىْ مَرَضِهٖ هٰذَا مَآدَّةً لِحَيٰوتِهٖ\nWAJ'AL MAA NAALAHOO FEE MARADIHEE HAADHAA MAADDATAN LIHAYAATIH\nMake what has befallen him in this illness a source of nourishment for his life\nوَكَفَّارَةً لِسَيِّئَاتِهٖ\nWA KAFFAARATAN LISAYYI'AATIH\nand an expiation for his sins.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ وَصَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَّاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nALLAAHUMMA WA SALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD\nO Allah, and bless Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad.\nIf this does not work, recite [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) 70 times.",
    "Verse of Healing\nRub the ailing part of the body with your hand and sincerely recite this verse of [Surah al-Isra](A21):\nوَنُنَزِّلُ مِنَ الْقُرْاٰنِ مَا هُوَ شِفَآءٌ وَّرَحْمَةٌ لِّلْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ\nWA NUNAZZILU MINAL QUR'AANI MAA HUWA SHIFAA'UN WA RAHMATUN LIL MU'MINEEN\nWe send down in the Quran that which is a cure and mercy for the faithful.",
    "Dua of Imam al-Reza for All Ailments\nيَا مُنْزِلَ الشِّفَاۤءِ وَمُذْهِبَ الدَّاۤءِ\nYAA MUNZILASH SHIFAA'I WA MUDH-HIBAD DAA'\nO He Who sends down healing and takes away disease,\nصَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَّاٰلِهٖ\nSALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIH\nbless Muhammad and his Household,\nوَاَنْزِلْ عَلٰى وَجَعِىْ الشِّفَاۤءَ\nWA ANZIL A'LAA WAJA'ISH SHIFAA'\nand send down healing upon my pain.",
    "Dua Taught by Jibril for Illness\nاِلٰهِىْ كُلَّمَا اَنْعَمْتَ عَلَىَّ نِعْمَةً قَلَّ لَكَ عِنْدَهَا شُكْرِىْ\nILAAHEE KULLAMAA AN'AMTA A'LAYYA NI'MATAN QALLA LAKA I'NDAHAA SHUKREE\nMy God, whenever You bestowed a blessing upon me, my gratitude to You for it fell short;\nوَكُلَّمَا ابْتَلَيْتَنِىْ بِبَلِيَّةٍ قَلَّ لَكَ عِنْدَهَا صَبْرِىْ\nWA KULLAMAB TALAYTANEE BIBALIYYATIN QALLA LAKA I'NDAHAA SABREE\nand whenever You tried me with an affliction, my patience for You in it fell short.\nفَيَا مَنْ قَلَّ شُكْرِىْ عِنْدَ نِعَمِهٖ فَلَمْ يَحْرِمْنِىْ\nFAYAA MAN QALLA SHUKREE I'NDA NI'AMIHEE FALAM YAHRIMNEE\nSo, O He before Whose blessings my gratitude fell short, yet He did not deprive me!\nوَيَا مَنْ قَلَّ صَبْرِىْ عِنْدَ بَلَاۤئِهٖ فَلَمْ يَخْذُلْنِىْ\nWA YAA MAN QALLA SABREE I'NDA BALAA'IHEE FALAM YAKHDHULNEE\nO He in Whose trials my patience fell short, yet He did not forsake me!\nوَيَا مَنْ رَّانِىْ عَلَى الْمَعَاصِىْ فَلَمْ يَفْضَحْنِىْ\nWA YAA MAR RAANEE A'LAL MA'AASEE FALAM YAFDAHNEE\nO He Who saw me committing sins, yet He did not disgrace me!\nوَيَا مَنْ رَّانِىْ عَلَى الْخَطَايَا فَلَمْ يُعَاقِبْنِىْ عَلَيْهَا\nWA YAA MAR RAANEE A'LAL KHATAAYAA FALAM YU'AAQIBNEE A'LAYHAA\nO He Who saw me committing wrongs, yet He did not punish me for them!\nصَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَّاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nSALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD\nBless Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad,\nوَّاغْفِرْ لِىْ ذَنْبِىْ وَاشْفِنِىْ مِنْ مَرَضِىْ\nWAGHFIR LEE DHANBEE WASHFINEE MIN MARADEE\nforgive me my sin, and heal me of my illness.\nاِنَّكَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَيْئٍ قَدِيْرٌ\nINNAKA A'LAA KULLI SHAY'IN QADEER\nSurely You have power over all things.",
    "Dua Found in al-Najashi's Bonnet\nبِسْمِ اللّٰهِ الْمَلِكِ الْحَقِّ الْمُبِيْنِ\nBISMILLAAHIL MALIKIL HAQQIL MUBEEN\nIn the Name of Allah, the King, the Manifest Truth.\nشَهِدَ اللّٰهُ اَنَّهٗ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ\nSHAHIDALLAAHU ANNAHOO LAA ILAAHA ILLAA HUW\nAllah bears witness that there is no god but He,\nوَالْمَلَاۤئِكَةُ وَاُوْلُوْا الْعِلْمِ قَاۤئِمًا بِالْقِسْطِ\nWAL MALAA'IKATU WA OOLUL I'LMI QAA'IMAN BIL QIST\nand so do the angels and those who possess knowledge, maintaining justice;\nلَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الْحَكِيْمُ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLAA HUWAL A'ZEEZUL HAKEEM\nthere is no god but He, the All-mighty, the All-wise.\nاِنَّ الدِّيْنَ عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ الْاِسْلَامُ\nINNAD DEENA I'NDALLAAHIL ISLAAM\nIndeed, with Allah religion is Islam.\nلِلّٰهِ نُوْرٌ وَّحِكْمَةٌ وَّحَوْلٌ وَّقُوَّةٌ وَّقُدْرَةٌ وَّسُلْطَانٌ وَّبُرْهَانٌ\nLILLAAHI NOORUN WA HIKMATUN WA HAWLUN WA QUWWATUN WA QUDRATUN WA SULTAANUN WA BURHAAN\nTo Allah belong light, wisdom, might, strength, power, authority and proof.\nلَّاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ اٰدَمُ صَفِىُّ اللّٰهِ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU AADAMU SAFIYYULLAAH\nThere is no god but Allah; Adam is the chosen one of Allah.\nلَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ اِبْرَاهِيْمُ خَلِيْلُ اللّٰهِ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU IBRAAHEEMU KHALEELULLAAH\nThere is no god but Allah; Abraham is the intimate friend of Allah.\nلَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ مُوْسٰى كَلِيْمُ اللّٰهِ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU MOOSAA KALEEMULLAAH\nThere is no god but Allah; Moses is the one to whom Allah spoke.\nلَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ مُحَمَّدٌ الْعَرَبِىُّ رَسُوْلُ اللّٰهِ وَحَبِيْبُهٗ وَخِيَرَتُهٗ مِنْ خَلْقِهٖ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU MUHAMMADUNIL A'RABIYYU RASOOLULLAAHI WA HABEEBUHOO WA KHIYARATUHOO MIN KHALQIH\nThere is no god but Allah; Muhammad the Arab is the Messenger of Allah, His beloved and His chosen one from His creation.\nاُسْكُنْ يَا جَمِيْعَ الْاَوْجَاعِ وَالْاَسْقَامِ وَالْاَمْرَاضِ وَجَمِيْعَ الْعِلَلِ وَجَمِيْعَ الْحُمَّيَاتِ\nUSKUN YAA JAMEE'AL AWJAA'I WAL ASQAAMI WAL AMRAADI WA JAMEE'AL I'LALI WA JAMEE'AL HUMMAYAAT\nBe still, O all pains, sicknesses and diseases, and all ailments and all fevers!\nسَكَّنْتُكَ بِالَّذِىْ سَكَنَ لَهٗ مَا فِى اللَّيْلِ وَالنَّهَارِ\nSAKKANTUKA BILLADHEE SAKANA LAHOO MAA FIL LAYLI WAN NAHAAR\nI still you by Him to Whom belongs whatever abides in the night and the day,\nوَهُوَ السَّمِيْعُ الْعَلِيْمُ\nWA HUWAS SAMEE'UL A'LEEM\nand He is the All-hearing, the All-knowing.\nوَصَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلٰى خَيْرِ خَلْقِهٖ مُحَمَّدٍ وَّاٰلِهٖ اَجْمَعِيْنَ\nWA SALLALLAAHU A'LAA KHAYRI KHALQIHEE MUHAMMADIN WA AALIHEE AJMA'EEN\nMay Allah bless the best of His creation, Muhammad, and all his Household.",
    "The Prophet's Amulet for Headache\nبِسْمِ اللّٰهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMILLAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful.\nلَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ الْمَلِكُ الْحَقُّ الْمُبِيْنُ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHUL MALIKUL HAQQUL MUBEEN\nThere is no god but Allah, the King, the Manifest Truth.\nشَهِدَ اللّٰهُ …\nSHAHIDALLAAHU …\nAllah bears witness ... (Qur'an 3:18)\nلِلّٰهِ نُوْرٌ وَّحِكْمَةٌ وَّعِزُّ وَقُوَّةٌ وَّبُرْهَانٌ وَّقُدْرَةٌ وَّسُلْطَانٌ وَّرَحْمَةٌ\nLILLAAHI NOORUN WA HIKMATUN WA I'ZZU WA QUWWATUN WA BURHAANUN WA QUDRATUN WA SULTAANUN WA RAHMAH\nTo Allah belong light, wisdom, honor, strength, proof, power, authority and mercy.\nيَّا مَنْ لَّا يَنَامُ\nYAA MAL LAA YANAAM\nO He Who never sleeps!\nلَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ اِبْرَاهِيْمُ خَلِيْلُ اللّٰهِ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU IBRAAHEEMU KHALEELULLAAH\nThere is no god but Allah; Abraham is the intimate friend of Allah.\nلَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ مُوْسٰى كَلِيْمُ اللّٰهِ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU MOOSAA KALEEMULLAAH\nThere is no god but Allah; Moses is the one to whom Allah spoke.\nلَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ عِيْسٰى رُوْحُ اللّٰهِ وَكَلِمَتُهٗ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU I'EESAA ROOHULLAAHI WA KALIMATUH\nThere is no god but Allah; Jesus is the Spirit of Allah and His Word.\nلَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ مُحَمَّدٌ رَّسُوْلُ اللّٰهِ وَصَفِيُّهٗ وَصِفْوَتُهٗ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLALLAAHU MUHAMMADUR RASOOLULLAAHI WA SAFIYYUHOO WA SIFWATUH\nThere is no god but Allah; Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, His chosen one and His elect;\nصَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَاٰلِهٖ وَسَلَّمَ\nSALLALLAAHU A'LAYHI WA AALIHEE WA SALLAM\nmay Allah bless him and his Household and grant them peace.\nاُسْكُنْ سَكَّنْتُكَ بِمَنْ يَّسْكُنُ لَهٗ مَا فِى السَّمٰوَاتِ وَالْاَرْضِ\nUSKUN SAKKANTUKA BIMAN YASKUNU LAHOO MAA FIS SAMAAWAATI WAL ARD\nBe still! I still you by Him for Whom all that is in the heavens and the earth is still,\nوَبِمَنْ سَكَنَ لَهٗ مَا فِى الَّيْلِ وَالنَّهَارِ\nWA BIMAN SAKANA LAHOO MAA FIL LAYLI WAN NAHAAR\nand by Him to Whom belongs whatever abides in the night and the day,\nوَهُوَ السَّمِيْعُ الْعَلِيْمُ\nWA HUWAS SAMEE'UL A'LEEM\nand He is the All-hearing, the All-knowing.\nفَسَخَّرْنَا لَهُ الرِّيْحَ تَجْرِىْ بِاَمْرِهٖ رُخَاۤءً حَيْثُ اَصَابَ\nFASAKHKHARNAA LAHUR REEHA TAJREE BI-AMRIHEE RUKHAA'AN HAYTHU ASAAB\nSo We disposed the wind for him, blowing softly wherever he intended by his command,\nوَالشَّيَاطِيْنَ كُلَّ بَنَّاۤءٍ وَغَوَّاصٍ\nWASH SHAYAATEENA KULLA BANNAA'IN WA GHAWWAAS\nand every builder and diver from the demons.\nاَلَاۤ اِلَى اللّٰهِ تَصِيْرُ الْاُمُوْرُ\nALAA ILALLAAHI TASEERUL UMOOR\nIndeed all matters return to Allah!"
  ],
  "merits": "Mother's Dua: It is reported that when a child is ailed, the mother may ascend to a roof, throw the head cover away, expose the hair of her head under the sky, prostrate herself, and say this supplication. The mother will not raise her head from the prostration but that her child is restored to health.\n\nAl-Fatihah over Water & Alms: Al-Shahid, may Allah have mercy upon him, has reported that whoever is tensely ailed may recite [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) forty times on a glass of water. He may then pour the water on his body. He may have a measure of wheat near him and hand over each beggar a measure and ask him to pray Almighty Allah to cure him. If he does so, he will be restored to health, Allah willing.\n\n“Medicate your patients with alms.” This saying is reported through considerable chains of authority.\n\nHolding the Patient's Right Arm: With reference to removal of diseases, al-Shahid has also reported that the right arm of a patient may be held while reciting [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) seven times. After that, this supplicatory prayer may be said. If this does not work, [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) may be repeated seventy times, and it will be effective, Allah willing.\n\nImam al-Baqir (a.s.) is reported to have said, “Whoever is not healed by [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) and [Surah al-Tawhid](A116), nothing else will heal him. Verily, these two Surahs cure of all ailments.”\n\nVerse of Healing: Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) is reported to have said: Allah will certainly cure any ailed believer who says this verse sincerely while rubbing his ailed organ with his hand.\n\nDua of Imam al-Reza: Imam al-Reza (a.s.) is reported to have said: For all ailments, you may say this supplicatory prayer.\n\nDua Taught by Jibril: Sayyid Ibn Tawus, may Allah have mercy upon him, has mentioned this narration in his book entitled Muhaj al-Da'awat: Ibn 'Abbas is reported to have said that he was once present with Imam Ali (a.s.) when a faint-faced man visited him and said, “O Commander of the Faithful, I am diseased person and many ailments and aches have afflicted me. So, please teach me a supplicatory prayer that helps me endure my ailments.” Answering him, Imam Ali (a.s.) said, “I will lead you to a supplicatory prayer that was taught by Archangel Gabriel to the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) when al-Hasan and al-Husayn fell ill.”\n\nIbn 'Abbas added: One year later, I saw the man fresh-faced and glowing. He said, “Whenever I said this supplicatory prayer in sickness, I would be soon restored to health, in ailment, I would be soon cured, and before a despotic authority, I would be protected against him.”\n\nAl-Najashi's Bonnet: It is reported that al-Najashi, an ancient king of Abyssinia, inherited from his fathers a four hundred year old bonnet that appeases any pain that it touches. When the bonnet was untied to inspect its secret, this supplicatory prayer was seen written therein.\n\nThe Prophet's Amulet: According to Makarim al-Akhlaq, al-Najashi, having had headache, wrote a message to the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) complaining about his ache. In response, the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) sent him a supplicatory amulet written in a patch. When al-Najashi put the patch in his bonnet, his headache was relieved."
}
